# Pinned as-is, and deliberately not a refusal. A depends_on naming no queued
# task reads as satisfied, because absence is the merge record — the branch that
# finishes a task deletes its file. So a dependency that has merged and a
# dependency misspelt are the same two lines in a checked-out tree, and telling
# them apart needs history this does not carry. That is queue review's job, not
# this one's.
run available
exit 0
file tasks/M1-02.md
	---
	id: M1-02
	owns:
	  - crates/normalize
	depends_on: [M1-01, M0-99]
	exclusive: no
	---
stdout
	M1-02
